rem Rational Zeros of a Function of
rem Three Variables
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=180
rem For fractions x, y, z of order Order
rem with x^(k+1) + y^(k+1) = z^(k+1) and
rem k = 1, 2, -1 or -2, sum the distinct
rem x + y + z and print numerator +
rem denominator

use algo
use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Order integer = 35

rem Write every fraction as X / L over
rem L = lcm(1..Order). Then z is x + y,
rem x y / (x + y), the root of x^2 + y^2
rem or x y over that root, kept when it
rem is itself a fraction on the list.
Ds = 2 to Order array
Rows = Ds len
Cols = Order - 1
L = (1 to Order array) lcm
Bm = Ds reshape Rows 1
Am = (1 to Cols array) reshape 1 Cols
Ok' = Am less Bm and (Am Bm gcd) equal 1
Xs = (Am * (L // Bm)) filter Ok array
N = Xs len
Cells = N * N
Xr = Xs reshape N 1
Yr = Xs reshape 1 N
Xf = (Xr + Yr * 0) reshape Cells
Yf = (Xr * 0 + Yr) reshape Cells
Known = new counter Xs
Prod = Xf * Yf
Root = (Xf * Xf + Yf * Yf) isqrt
Sq = Root * Root equal Xf * Xf + Yf * Yf
Z1 = Xf + Yf
Z2 = Root
Z3 = Prod // Z1
Z4 = Prod // (Root max 1)
E3' = Prod mod Z1 equal 0
E4' = Prod mod (Root max 1) equal 0
H1' = Known Z1 greater 0
H2' = Sq and Known Z2 greater 0
H3' = E3 and Known Z3 greater 0
H4' = Sq and E4 and Known Z4 greater 0
S1' = (Z1 + Z1) filter H1 array
S2' = (Z1 + Z2) filter H2 array
S3' = (Z1 + Z3) filter H3 array
S4' = (Z1 + Z4) filter H4 array
All' = concat S1 S2 S3 S4 unique
Total = All sum
G = Total L gcd
Answer = Total // G + L // G
Answer print
